{
  "id": "ss.enemy.ovum",
  "name": "Ovum",
  "description": "What the Matriarch lays: one of the pink shapes drifting inside her brood chamber, put down on the floor. A single rigid egg of her own $pheromone sitting in a smear of jelly, with the thing inside showing through — a curled grub, already carrying a lit organ, because what she lays now is marked. The only body on the roster that does not move of its own accord: it rocks. It is two pieces already — a cup and a cap, meeting along a hairline crack round the upper third — and that is where it opens. The game draws it in place of the young for the hatch window, sized to what is coming out, so a Bulwark's egg is visibly bigger than a Replete's. Idle (`rock`) is the egg rocking on the jelly with the grub turning inside — the one thing on the field that says 'about to'. `death` is the hatch or the kill, the same break either way: the cap kicks off along the crack, the dark of the empty cup shows where it was, what was inside is gone, the cup settles and the jelly spreads.",
